e ice cream it's the one thing that  so many people have so much emotions  tied into  it's a total equalizer ice cream keith  says  even taught her to think differently and  try new things  she became the first in her family to go  to college  i had worked my way up out of business  school  worked for some fortune 100 companies i  ended up running a 70 million dollar  business  and i ended up in the food industry of  all things i had the dream job  i had the dream career i was making more  money in a year than my dad did in 20.  and it's funny sometimes you get there  and it's not all that it's cracked up to  be  at age 38 while on a girl's trip  keefe had an epiphany i just broke down  and i said i am miserable and i was so  lonely  my really close girlfriend turns to me  and she says quit  and i said what would i do  and my other girlfriend turns to me and  she's like you're always complaining our  neighborhood doesn't have an ice cream  shop  and you make the best ice cream in the  world  she's like why don't you open an ice  cream shop and so literally that weekend  we wrote my business plan put together  my deck ran my financials  and two weeks later i resigned weren't  you scared i was  more scared to not change my life and to  continue being unhappy  keefe took her corporate-built savings  and bet on herself  launching clementine's creamery my  approach to clementines was  i am going to do things different i am  going to make ice cream the way it was  made  50 75 years ago i'm going to open a  micro creamery  and there are people who are saying i  don't know what a micro creamery is i  know what a micro brewery is what's a  micro creamery so think micro brewery  for beer but for ice cream in the  simplest terms the ice cream is made in  small batches by real people  a process we got to see and be a part of  at clementine's st  louis based kitchen it's usually two  people because we're moving quick and we  go between machines  got it it has to be all natural and  anything in it like the gooey butter  cake here in one of clementine's  signature flavors  has to be handmade the ice cream also  has to have  less than 30 percent air mixed in it  might be a little fudge  so can i go back in yeah what a shock  that i put maybe too much in there  and contain more than 16 butter fat  numbers that may be tough to digest  until you take a taste  i mean i'm a kid all over again it's  amazing  and so the butter fat is what coats your  tongue  and allows the flavor to linger in your  mouth  it creates a super satiating effect i'm  not sharing  i'm not sharing with anybody  clementine's flavors take you on  a sensory journey salted cracker caramel  and italian butter cookie  three different kinds of crackers chunks  of deliciousness  oh my god vegan options lemon poppy seed  and coconut chocolate fudge  there's even a naughty line of ice cream  that's alcohol infused  i mean that's a manhattan that is a  manhattan wow  boozy beautiful crisp but that's not all  for keith the experience the emotion  she's trying to create for each customer  starts even before the first scoop  we have crafted an experience for people  who come into our shops  to make it one that's memorable to make  it one that they love  and they open the door and they step  over the magic threshold  they take a breath of the fresh waffle  cones  and they look around and their their  face brightens and they get a smile on  their face that's  before they even take a bite of ice  cream it's before they ever take the  bite of ice cream because they know  once they step over that magic threshold  their life  is going to be better than it was before  just like keefe's i work harder now  than i ever have i work 24 hours a day  seven days a week  but it's different because it's mine and  it's my team  and it's my people and they're my  customers and there you are  thank you absolutely and i'm so proud  of what we're doing and what we're  building and what's that old adage  when